#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:2
msgid "Firmware updates and recovery"
msgstr "Ažuriranja firmvera i oporavak"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:4
msgid ""
"The Viewer keeps the camera's firmware manager, so a device can be recovered"
" or re-provisioned in the field without the full IDE. It bundles the "
"matching firmware release for every board and the loaders for every board "
"family's bootloader, and it detects the board and speaks the right protocol "
"without being told."
msgstr ""
"Viewer zadržava kamerin upravitelj firmvera, pa se uređaj može oporaviti ili"
" ponovno pripremiti na terenu bez cjelovitog IDE-a. Uključuje odgovarajuće "
"izdanje firmvera za svaku pločicu i učitavače za bootloader svake obitelji "
"pločica te prepoznaje pločicu i govori ispravnim protokolom bez uputa."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:11
msgid ""
"Unlike the IDE, the Viewer does not nag to update: so a demonstration is "
"never interrupted by an out-of-date prompt, whatever firmware the product "
"ships stays in place. The firmware operations are available on demand from "
"the Tools menu when you do want them."
msgstr ""
"Za razliku od IDE-a, Viewer ne dosađuje s ažuriranjima: pa demonstraciju "
"nikad ne prekida upit o zastarjelosti, a firmver koji proizvod isporučuje "
"ostaje na mjestu. Operacije s firmverom dostupne su na zahtjev iz izbornika "
"Tools kada ih zatrebate."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:18
msgid "Loading firmware"
msgstr "Učitavanje firmvera"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:20
msgid ""
"Tools → Load Custom Firmware flashes a firmware binary -- or a board's "
"build-output ``.zip`` bundle -- from disk, the way to put a product's own "
"firmware onto a replacement camera. The dialog offers the same options as "
"the IDE's: erase the internal flash filesystem, and reset the ROM file "
"system."
msgstr ""
"Tools → Load Custom Firmware upisuje binarnu datoteku firmvera -- ili "
"``.zip`` paket izlaza izgradnje pločice -- s diska, način da vlastiti "
"firmver proizvoda stavite na zamjensku kameru. Dijaloški okvir nudi iste "
"opcije kao IDE: brisanje internog flash datotečnog sustava i ponovno "
"postavljanje ROM datotečnog sustava."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:28
msgid "Loading a ROM file system"
msgstr "Učitavanje ROM datotečnog sustava"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:30
msgid ""
"Tools → Load ROMFS onto OpenMV Cam writes a ``.img`` ROM file system image "
"-- a product's models and assets -- to the camera, so the Viewer can restore"
" a device's data as well as its firmware."
msgstr ""
"Tools → Load ROMFS onto OpenMV Cam upisuje ``.img`` sliku ROM datotečnog "
"sustava -- modele i resurse proizvoda -- na kameru, pa Viewer može vratiti "
"podatke uređaja kao i njegov firmver."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:36
msgid "Recovering a bricked camera"
msgstr "Oporavak neispravne kamere"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:38
msgid ""
"A camera whose firmware is broken enough that it no longer shows up as a "
"serial port can still be saved, because the bootloader sits below the "
"firmware and survives anything short of hardware damage. When connect finds "
"no camera, the Viewer asks whether a bricked camera is attached and walks "
"you through recovery: you select the board type, the Viewer drives the "
"board's bootloader interface, and the bundled release firmware goes on. "
"Tools → Force enter OpenMV Cam bootloader does the reboot-into-bootloader "
"step explicitly for a camera that still connects."
msgstr ""
"Kamera čiji je firmver toliko oštećen da se više ne prikazuje kao serijski "
"priključak i dalje se može spasiti jer se bootloader nalazi ispod firmvera i"
" preživljava sve osim hardverskog oštećenja. Kada povezivanje ne pronađe "
"kameru, Viewer pita je li priključena neispravna kamera i vodi vas kroz "
"oporavak: odaberete vrstu pločice, Viewer upravlja bootloader sučeljem "
"pločice i uključeni firmver izdanja se postavlja. Tools → Force enter OpenMV"
" Cam bootloader izričito izvodi korak ponovnog pokretanja u bootloader za "
"kameru koja se još povezuje."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:18
msgid "Third-party boards and fleet updates"
msgstr "Ažuriranja ploča i flote trećih strana"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/viewer/firmware.rst:20
msgid ""
"The Viewer supports :doc:`third-party repositories <../ide/third-party-"
"repositories>`, so a company shipping its own board in its own Viewer can "
"keep a fleet of those cameras current in the field. This is the one "
"exception to the no-nagging rule: a third-party board *does* get the out-of-"
"date prompt and updates through the Viewer, because the update is the "
"vendor's own -- served from the URL in the repository's manifest, not from "
"OpenMV. OpenMV's own boards still never prompt. The Viewer checks a "
"repository's firmware channel at launch and offers newer firmware when the "
"vendor publishes it; it does not pull down the examples, models, or stubs a "
"repository may also carry, since the Viewer has no interface for them."
msgstr ""
"Preglednik podržava :doc:`third-party repositories <../ide/third-party-"
"repositories>`, tako da tvrtka koja isporučuje vlastitu ploču u vlastitom "
"pregledniku može održavati flotu tih kamera aktualnom na terenu. Ovo je "
"jedina iznimka od pravila bez prigovaranja: ploča treće strane *does* dobiva"
" zastarjelu obavijest i ažuriranja putem Preglednika, jer je ažuriranje "
"vlastito dobavljača -- poslužuje se s URL-a u manifestu repozitorija, a ne "
"iz OpenMV-a. OpenMV-ove vlastite ploče još uvijek nikad ne traže upit. "
"Preglednik provjerava firmware kanal repozitorija pri pokretanju i nudi "
"noviji firmware kada ga prodavač objavi; ne povlači primjere, modele ili "
"zaglavke koje spremište također može sadržavati, budući da Preglednik nema "
"sučelje za njih."
